st-macos - simple terminal for macOS
------------------------------------
A fork of st, the simple terminal emulator which sucks less, with
the X11 frontend replaced by a native Cocoa one. No XQuartz needed.

st.c (VT parser, pty handling, screen state) is upstream st with the
scrollback patch applied. mac.m replaces x.c and implements the
win.h interface with AppKit.

Requirements
------------
macOS with the Xcode command line tools:

    xcode-select --install


Configuration
-------------
In the spirit of suckless there are no config files. Edit the
"appearance" block at the top of mac.m (font, colors, selection
color, window size, title) and recompile.


Installation
------------
    make clean
    make

Then copy the st binary anywhere in your $PATH, e.g.:

    cp st ~/.local/bin/


Running st
----------
st sets TERM to xterm-256color, which macOS ships with, so no
terminfo setup is required.


Credits
-------
Based on st from suckless.org (https://st.suckless.org) and the
st scrollback patch. st is based on Aurélien APTEL
<aurelien dot aptel at gmail dot com> bt source code.
